From b5addce6e55e28100bf3c9a7e752b8e9a178a4f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeheartgold-3ds-bootstrap <bootstrap@invalid>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 17:30:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PPW lobby players: write the PlayerRecord designators in
 declaration order

src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp:46 builds a PlayerRecord with
`(PlayerRecord) { .channel = ..., .timeLow = ..., .timeHigh = ... }`. The
struct declares `u32 timeLow, timeHigh; int channel;` (:12-15), so the
designators are out of order, and GCC's C++ designated-initializer support
requires declaration order: "designator order for field 'PlayerRecord::timeLow'
does not match declaration order". MWCC accepted the C form.

Under SDK_PORT_3DS list .timeLow, .timeHigh, .channel; each field has an
explicit designator, so the values and the resulting record are identical.
The #else keeps the original order for the DS build.

gcc-10 -E -P without SDK_PORT_3DS: byte-identical (36305 bytes both).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp b/src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp
index 8d09461..4c2d169 100644
--- a/src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp
+++ b/src/lobby/ppw_lobby_players_update_states.cpp
@@ -43,7 +43,13 @@ void PPWLobbyPlayers_UpdateStates(PPWLobbyPlayers *players) {
                 player->systemProfileChanged = notChanged;
                 profilePlayer = PlayerAt(it);
                 profilePlayer->userProfileChanged = notChanged;
+#ifdef SDK_PORT_3DS
+                // C++ designated initializers must follow declaration order
+                // (timeLow, timeHigh, channel); the values are unchanged.
+                const PlayerRecord &recordRef = (PlayerRecord) { .timeLow = ((u32 *)&player->systemProfile.time)[0], .timeHigh = ((u32 *)&player->systemProfile.time)[1], .channel = player->systemProfile.channel };
+#else
                 const PlayerRecord &recordRef = (PlayerRecord) { .channel = player->systemProfile.channel, .timeLow = ((u32 *)&player->systemProfile.time)[0], .timeHigh = ((u32 *)&player->systemProfile.time)[1] };
+#endif
                 PlayerRecord record = recordRef;
                 userProfileSize = profilePlayer->userProfile.size;
                 id = PlayerAt(it)->id;
